// RosettaForge — Architecture
// ===========================
//
// Layout (every tracked file ends in .gable):
//
//   START.gable / LICENSE.gable / ARCHITECTURE.gable / CONTRIBUTING.gable /
//   GABLE_COMPATIBILITY.gable / PROGRESS.gable
//   core/main.gable            CLI entry point (one `main`, bounded imports)
//   core/catalog.gable         Entry struct and catalog helpers
//   core/search.gable          keyword search over index shards
//   core/filters.gable         category / language / difficulty filters
//   core/viewer.gable          specimen metadata display
//   core/scoring.gable         verification scoring helpers
//   core/validation.gable      input and argument validation
//   library/*/                 reusable Gable primitives (no `main`)
//   languages/*/               reference-language profiles
//   challenges/*/              challenge specimens, each with its own `main`
//   index/catalog_NNN.gable    bounded index shards: metadata only, [Entry] data
//   verification/*/            test drivers and verification records
//   benchmarks/*, documentation/*, experiments/*
//
// Compilation boundaries (verified against Gable v0.3, commit
// 58405ffd9a6e9201ae7e355faf8e6002de721034):
//
//   * One program = root file + every imported file, transitively.
//   * Maximum 512 source files per compilation.
//   * Maximum import depth 64.
//   * Single program-wide namespace: no duplicate declaration names.
//   * 64 MiB per file, 256 MiB total per compilation.
//
// Design rules
// ------------
//
//   1. NEVER compile all 10,000 challenge files into one executable.
//      Every challenge specimen is a standalone program with its own `main`
//      and imports nothing (or almost nothing), so each compilation is one file.
//
//   2. The CLI imports only index shards (metadata), never challenge files.
//      Shards stay small (a few hundred entries each); total import graph stays
//      far below 512 files and depth 64.

//   3. Each index shard declares its own entry-list variable
//      (catalog_000, catalog_001, ...). The Entry struct is declared once in
//      core/catalog.gable. Shard file names and variable names are unique.
//
//   4. Gable cannot spawn child processes. The CLI prints the exact command to
//      run or check a specimen; the user runs it directly.
//
//   5. All executable project logic is Gable. Other languages appear only as
//      escaped reference snippets inside Gable strings or comments.
//
//   6. No mutable global state beyond catalog data; functions are pure where
//      practical; file I/O uses fs_read_text / fs_write_text_atomic only in
//      tools, never in challenge specimens.
//
//   7. Deterministic, idempotent generation: re-running the generator produces
//      identical files; validated files are never overwritten.
//
//   8. Avoid O(n^2) string concatenation in loops: collect [str] and .join().
//
//   9. Respect int wrapping, truncating division, division-by-zero trap (exit
//      70), byte-length string semantics, and bounds-checked indexing.
//
//   10. Library modules have no `main`; they are verified through small driver
//       programs in verification/ that import them.
